                <pb facs="0740" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.6363 Barco/123: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Piles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-08-01T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>63. Department’s 40, July 27, 6 p.m. I had an interview with President this
                    afternoon and left with him a copy of note. I referred to opinion of Minister of
                    Industry that decree is not sustainable and to Colombia-Venezuelan arbitration
                    and urged rescission of decree. He seemed impressed and promised a decision
                    early next week.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Piles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
